{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Introduction to PyTorch Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "A 3-layer MLP trained on MNIST using only PyTorch primitives. No high-level wrappers. No `torchvision.datasets`. We download and parse the raw data ourselves."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: Load MNIST From Raw Files"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "MNIST ships as 4 gzipped files: training images (60,000 x 28 x 28), training labels, test images (10,000 x 28 x 28), test labels. We download them and parse the binary format."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import torch"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import torch.nn as nn"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import struct"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import gzip"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import urllib.request"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import os"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def download_mnist(path=\"./mnist_data\"):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    base_url = \"https://storage.googleapis.com/cvdf-datasets/mnist/\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    files = ["
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"train-images-idx3-ubyte.gz\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"train-labels-idx1-ubyte.gz\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"t10k-images-idx3-ubyte.gz\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"t10k-labels-idx1-ubyte.gz\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    ]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    os.makedirs(path, exist_ok=True)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for f in files:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        filepath = os.path.join(path, f)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if not os.path.exists(filepath):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            urllib.request.urlretrieve(base_url + f, filepath)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def load_images(filepath):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    with gzip.open(filepath, \"rb\") as f:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        magic, num, rows, cols = struct.unpack(\">IIII\", f.read(16))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        data = f.read()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        images = torch.frombuffer(bytearray(data), dtype=torch.uint8)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        images = images.reshape(num, rows * cols).float() / 255.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return images"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def load_labels(filepath):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    with gzip.open(filepath, \"rb\") as f:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        magic, num = struct.unpack(\">II\", f.read(8))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        data = f.read()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        labels = torch.frombuffer(bytearray(data), dtype=torch.uint8).long()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return labels"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: Define the Model"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "A 3-layer MLP: 784 -> 256 -> 128 -> 10. ReLU activations. Dropout for regularization. No batch norm to keep it simple."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class MNISTModel(nn.Module):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        super().__init__()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.net = nn.Sequential("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.Linear(784, 256),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.ReLU(),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.Dropout(0.2),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.Linear(256, 128),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.ReLU(),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.Dropout(0.2),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.Linear(128, 10),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        )"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def forward(self, x):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return self.net(x)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The output layer produces 10 raw logits (one per digit). No softmax -- `CrossEntropyLoss` handles that internally."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Parameter count: 784*256 + 256 + 256*128 + 128 + 128*10 + 10 = 235,146. Tiny by modern standards. GPT-2 small has 124M. This trains in seconds."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: Training Loop"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The canonical forward-loss-backward-step pattern."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def train_one_epoch(model, loader, criterion, optimizer, device):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    model.train()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    total_loss = 0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    correct = 0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    total = 0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for images, labels in loader:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        images, labels = images.to(device), labels.to(device)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        optimizer.zero_grad()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        outputs = model(images)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        loss = criterion(outputs, labels)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        loss.backward()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        optimizer.step()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        total_loss += loss.item() * images.size(0)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        _, predicted = outputs.max(1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        correct += predicted.eq(labels).sum().item()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        total += labels.size(0)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return total_loss / total, correct / total"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def evaluate(model, loader, criterion, device):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    model.eval()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    total_loss = 0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    correct = 0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    total = 0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    with torch.no_grad():"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for images, labels in loader:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            images, labels = images.to(device), labels.to(device)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            outputs = model(images)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            loss = criterion(outputs, labels)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            total_loss += loss.item() * images.size(0)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            _, predicted = outputs.max(1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            correct += predicted.eq(labels).sum().item()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            total += labels.size(0)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return total_loss / total, correct / total"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Note `torch.no_grad()` during evaluation. This disables autograd, reducing memory usage and speeding up inference. Without it, PyTorch builds a computational graph you never use."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: Wire Everything Together"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def main():"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    device = torch.device(\"cuda\" if torch.cuda.is_available() else \"cpu\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    download_mnist()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    train_images = load_images(\"./mnist_data/train-images-idx3-ubyte.gz\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    train_labels = load_labels(\"./mnist_data/train-labels-idx1-ubyte.gz\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    test_images = load_images(\"./mnist_data/t10k-images-idx3-ubyte.gz\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    test_labels = load_labels(\"./mnist_data/t10k-labels-idx1-ubyte.gz\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    train_dataset = torch.utils.data.TensorDataset(train_images, train_labels)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    test_dataset = torch.utils.data.TensorDataset(test_images, test_labels)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    train_loader = torch.utils.data.DataLoader("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        train_dataset, batch_size=64, shuffle=True"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    )"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    test_loader = torch.utils.data.DataLoader("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        test_dataset, batch_size=256, shuffle=False"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    )"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    model = MNISTModel().to(device)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    criterion = nn.CrossEntropyLoss()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    optimizer = torch.optim.Adam(model.parameters(), lr=1e-3)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    num_params = sum(p.numel() for p in model.parameters())"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(f\"Device: {device}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(f\"Parameters: {num_params:,}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(f\"Train samples: {len(train_dataset):,}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(f\"Test samples: {len(test_dataset):,}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for epoch in range(10):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        train_loss, train_acc = train_one_epoch("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            model, train_loader, criterion, optimizer, device"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        )"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        test_loss, test_acc = evaluate("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            model, test_loader, criterion, device"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        )"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        print("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            f\"Epoch {epoch+1:2d} | \""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            f\"Train Loss: {train_loss:.4f} | Train Acc: {train_acc:.4f} | \""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            f\"Test Loss: {test_loss:.4f} | Test Acc: {test_acc:.4f}\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        )"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    torch.save(model.state_dict(), \"mnist_mlp.pt\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(f\"\\nModel saved to mnist_mlp.pt\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(f\"Final test accuracy: {test_acc:.4f}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Expected output after 10 epochs: ~97.8% test accuracy. Training time on CPU: ~30 seconds. On GPU: ~5 seconds. On your mini framework with the same architecture: ~45 minutes."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. **Add batch normalization.** Insert `nn.BatchNorm1d` after each linear layer (before the activation). Compare test accuracy and training speed vs the dropout-only version. Batch norm should reach 98%+ in fewer epochs.\n\n2. **Implement a learning rate finder.** Train for one epoch with exponentially increasing learning rate (from 1e-7 to 1.0). Plot loss vs LR. The optimal LR is just before the loss starts climbing. Use this to pick a better LR for the MNIST model.\n\n3. **Port to GPU with mixed precision.** Add `torch.amp.autocast` and `GradScaler` to the training loop. Measure throughput (samples/second) with and without mixed precision on GPU. On an A100, expect ~2x speedup.\n\n4. **Build a custom Dataset.** Download Fashion-MNIST (same format as MNIST but with clothing items). Implement a `FashionMNISTDataset(Dataset)` class with `__getitem__` and `__len__`. Train the same MLP and compare accuracy. Fashion-MNIST is harder -- expect ~88% vs ~98%.\n\n5. **Replace Adam with SGD + momentum.** Train with `SGD(params, lr=0.01, momentum=0.9)`. Compare convergence curves. Then add a `CosineAnnealingLR` scheduler and see if SGD catches up to Adam by epoch 10."
      ]
    }
  ],
